 "poem": "This is my poor heart's life, o'er sixty years,\nThe love I had for thee; it has given\nTo me this love and sorrow.\nVI. Now the war-souls that sleep below\nCome to us now: our flowers awake,\nAnd all our hopes are blown out again,\nAs from the sunburnt dream of our\nMarching thro' the world so glorious far\nIn battle with a lion-king's heart;\nBut shall we talk what they cannot\nSpeak? And not to speak of our\nFlowers in the wild on many far",
